## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA workflow for data privacy policy failures, including evidence capture and cross-tenant rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling for evidence and artifacts
- Lifecycle state machine and ownership
- Minimal REST API design with linked logs/traces
- Tenant/region metrics for containment and recurrence
- RCA templates and canary rollout planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// CAPA core types (overview)
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidence: string[];
  artifacts: string[];
  state: 'detected'|'triaged'|'in_progress'|'contained'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt?: string;
  links?: { type: string; url: string }[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale CAPA data stores across regions?
- How to ensure regulatory auditability and evidence integrity?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical CAPA program around data privacy, tenant isolation, and controlled policy changes in real-time fintech systems.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model: evidence, lineage, owners, policy references
- Tenant-aware lifecycle: detect, contain, remediate, verify with SLAs
- Minimal API: create/update CAPAs with logs/traces, policy links
- Metrics: containment time, recurrence rate, tenant impact
- RCA and canary rollback: structured **root cause** templates and safe rollout controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sketch: POST /api/capa
app.post('/api/capa', (req, res) => {
  const {evidence, lineage, owners, policyLink, tenantId} = req.body;
  // validate inputs, create CAPA, emit logs, assign owners
  res.status(201).json({capaId: 'CAPA-1234'});
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce tenant isolation in evidence and logs metadata?
- What would be your go/no-go criteria for canary rollback validation?
